  <section class="section" id="principles" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
        <div class="section-mark"><span class="numeral">02</span><p class="eyebrow">Principles</p></div>
        <h2 id="principles-title">Seven Principles for Governed Enterprise AI.</h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="principles" role="list">
        <li class="principle"><h3>Operate through governed interfaces.</h3><p>AI reaches enterprise systems through defined tools and APIs with scopes and limits. Not through shared credentials, screen automation or direct database access.</p></li>
        <li class="principle"><h3>Keep business calculations deterministic.</h3><p>Prices, margins, quantities, tax and balances are computed in versioned, tested code. The model can explain a result; it does not produce it.</p></li>
        <li class="principle"><h3>Read before write.</h3><p>An agent reads the current state of the system before it proposes a change, and the proposal is expressed as a difference from that state.</p></li>
        <li class="principle"><h3>Validate before execution.</h3><p>Every proposed action passes schema, policy and limit checks before anything runs. A failed check stops the action and says why.</p></li>
        <li class="principle"><h3>Approve by risk.</h3><p>Low-risk actions run within policy. High-risk actions wait for explicit approval from a named role, and the approval is recorded with the action.</p></li>
        <li class="principle"><h3>Verify independently.</h3><p>After execution, a separate check reads the system back and compares the result with the intent. Sending a command is not the same as success.</p></li>
        <li class="principle"><h3>Keep evidence and state auditable.</h3><p>Sources, calculations, approvals and the resulting system state are stored per action, in a form internal audit and security can read.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band-dark" id="stack" aria-labelledby="stack-title">
